<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    FLAMEFANG_SNAKE_REBIRTH_1 — owner sheet note, 2026-09-16, verbatim:
    "rename this to Flamefang and make it venomous." Swaps GR_Boomsnake's
    bite tool from GeneticRim's own capacity (GR_VeryToxicBite, which
    already injects vanilla ToxicBuildup at 0.005 severity/damage — RimSage/
    grep-verified this pass against the donor mod's own
    Defs/DamageDefs/Damages_LocalInjury.xml, Defs/Maneuvers/Maneuvers.xml
    and Defs/ToolCapacityDefs/ToolCapacity.xml) onto this campaign's own
    RUT_FlamefangBite capacity, which routes to RUT_FlamefangVenomBite ->
    RUT_FlamefangVenom (Defs/HediffDefs, Defs/DamageDefs, Defs/
    ToolCapacityDefs — same load, this mod's own always-loaded Defs) instead
    — a flavor-distinct burning venom, not a reskin of generic toxic
    buildup, matching the new fire-follower identity from
    Patches/FlamefangIdentity.xml.

    Only the bite tool's <capacities><li> entry is touched; power,
    cooldownTime, linkedBodyPartsGroup and the surpriseAttack stun all stay
    the donor's own values. The second ("head", Blunt) tool is untouched.

    PatchOperationConditional guards the exact node so an upstream GR_
    Boomsnake rework that changes its own capacity string becomes a silent
    no-op here rather than a red launch error.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Genetics Expanded</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="GR_Boomsnake"]/tools/li/capacities/li[.="GR_VeryToxicBite"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
        <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="GR_Boomsnake"]/tools/li/capacities/li[.="GR_VeryToxicBite"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <li>RUT_FlamefangBite</li>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
